# Angular Code Style Guidelines

Based on the [official Angular style guide](https://angular.dev/style-guide).

## File Structure & Naming

### File Naming Conventions
- **Separate words with hyphens**: `user-profile.ts`, `ticket-list.component.ts`
- **Tests end with `.spec.ts`**: `user-profile.spec.ts`
- **Match file name to TypeScript identifier**: `UserProfile` → `user-profile.ts`
- **Component files share the same name**: `user-profile.ts`, `user-profile.html`, `user-profile.css`

### Avoid Generic File Names
```typescript
// Bad
helpers.ts
utils.ts
common.ts

// Good
date-formatting.ts
ticket-validators.ts
api-error-handling.ts
```

### Project Structure
```
src/
├── main.ts                   # Bootstrap file (required name)
├── app/
│   ├── app.component.ts
│   ├── app.routes.ts
│   └── [feature-areas]/      # Organize by feature, NOT by type
```

### Organize by Feature, NOT by Type
```typescript
// Bad - grouping by type
src/
├── components/
│   ├── ticket-list.component.ts
│   └── ticket-card.component.ts
├── services/
│   └── ticket.service.ts
├── directives/
│   └── highlight.directive.ts

// Good - grouping by feature
src/
├── tickets/
│   ├── ticket-list.component.ts
│   ├── ticket-list.component.html
│   ├── ticket-list.component.spec.ts
│   ├── ticket-card.component.ts
│   ├── ticket.service.ts
│   └── highlight.directive.ts
├── projects/
│   ├── project-list.component.ts
│   └── project.service.ts
```

### One Concept Per File
- One component, directive, or service per file
- Keep files small and focused
- If code doesn't fit a common theme, split into multiple files

## Components

### Component Class Organization
```typescript
import { Component, OnInit, OnDestroy, input, output, computed, inject } from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-ticket-list',
  imports: [CommonModule],
  templateUrl: './ticket-list.component.html',
  styleUrl: './ticket-list.component.css',
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
})
export class TicketListComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy {
  // 1. Injected dependencies (using inject function)
  private readonly ticketService = inject(TicketService);
  private readonly route = inject(ActivatedRoute);

  // 2. Inputs (readonly)
  readonly projectId = input.required<string>();
  readonly initialFilters = input<TicketFilters>();

  // 3. Outputs (readonly)
  readonly ticketSelected = output<Ticket>();

  // 4. Queries (readonly)
  readonly ticketCards = viewChildren(TicketCardComponent);

  // 5. Internal state - use protected for template-only members
  protected tickets = signal<Ticket[]>([]);
  protected loading = signal(false);
  protected readonly openTicketCount = computed(() => 
    this.tickets().filter(t => t.status !== 'done').length
  );

  // 6. Private properties
  private readonly destroy$ = new Subject<void>();

  // 7. Lifecycle hooks - implement interfaces, keep simple
  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.initializeData();
    this.setupSubscriptions();
  }

  ngOnDestroy(): void {
    this.destroy$.next();
    this.destroy$.complete();
  }

  // 8. Protected methods (called from template)
  protected onTicketClick(ticket: Ticket): void {
    this.ticketSelected.emit(ticket);
  }

  // 9. Private methods
  private initializeData(): void {
    // Logic extracted from ngOnInit
  }

  private setupSubscriptions(): void {
    // Logic extracted from ngOnInit
  }
}
```

### Use `readonly` for Angular-Initialized Properties
```typescript
// Inputs, outputs, and queries should be readonly
readonly userId = input<string>();
readonly userSaved = output<void>();
readonly userName = model<string>();
readonly paymentMethods = viewChildren(PaymentMethodComponent);
```

### Use `protected` for Template-Only Members
```typescript
@Component({
  template: `<p>{{ fullName() }}</p>`,
})
export class UserProfile {
  readonly firstName = input<string>();
  readonly lastName = input<string>();

  // Not part of public API, but used in template
  protected fullName = computed(() => `${this.firstName()} ${this.lastName()}`);
}
```

### Lifecycle Hook Interfaces
```typescript
// Always implement lifecycle interfaces
import { Component, OnInit, OnDestroy, AfterViewInit } from '@angular/core';

@Component({/*...*/})
export class TicketListComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy, AfterViewInit {
  ngOnInit(): void {}
  ngAfterViewInit(): void {}
  ngOnDestroy(): void {}
}
```

### Keep Lifecycle Hooks Simple
```typescript
// Bad - complex logic inline
ngOnInit() {
  this.logger.setMode('info');
  this.logger.monitorErrors();
  this.http.get('/api/tickets').subscribe(/*...*/);
  this.route.params.pipe(/*...*/).subscribe(/*...*/);
  // ...20 more lines
}

// Good - delegate to well-named methods
ngOnInit() {
  this.initializeLogging();
  this.loadTickets();
  this.watchRouteChanges();
}
```

## Dependency Injection

### Prefer `inject()` Over Constructor Injection
```typescript
// Preferred
export class TicketService {
  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);
  private readonly config = inject(ConfigService);
  private readonly logger = inject(LoggerService);
}

// Avoid
export class TicketService {
  constructor(
    private readonly http: HttpClient,
    private readonly config: ConfigService,
    private readonly logger: LoggerService,
  ) {}
}
```

Benefits of `inject()`:
- More readable with many dependencies
- Easier to add comments
- Better type inference
- No separation between declaration and initialization

## Templates

### Prefer `class` and `style` Over `ngClass` and `ngStyle`
```html
<!-- Preferred -->
<div [class.admin]="isAdmin" [class.dense]="density === 'high'">
<div [style.color]="textColor" [style.background-color]="backgroundColor">

<!-- Also acceptable -->
<div [class]="{admin: isAdmin, dense: density === 'high'}">
<div [style]="{'color': textColor, 'background-color': backgroundColor}">

<!-- Avoid -->
<div [ngClass]="{admin: isAdmin, dense: density === 'high'}">
<div [ngStyle]="{'color': textColor, 'background-color': backgroundColor}">
```

### Use Control Flow Syntax (Angular 17+)
```html
@if (loading()) {
  <app-spinner />
} @else if (error()) {
  <app-error [message]="error()" />
} @else {
  @for (ticket of tickets(); track ticket.id) {
    <app-ticket-card 
      [ticket]="ticket" 
      (click)="selectTicket(ticket)" 
    />
  } @empty {
    <p>No tickets found</p>
  }
}
```

### Name Event Handlers for What They DO
```html
<!-- Good - describes the action -->
<button (click)="saveTicket()">Save</button>
<button (click)="deleteTicket()">Delete</button>
<input (blur)="validateEmail()">

<!-- Bad - describes the event -->
<button (click)="handleClick()">Save</button>
<button (click)="onClick()">Delete</button>
<input (blur)="onBlur()">
```

For keyboard events with modifiers:
```html
<textarea 
  (keydown.control.enter)="submitForm()" 
  (keydown.escape)="cancelEdit()"
>
```

### Avoid Complex Logic in Templates
```html
<!-- Bad - complex expression -->
<div>{{ tickets.filter(t => t.status === 'open' && t.priority === 'high').length }}</div>

<!-- Good - use computed signal -->
<div>{{ urgentTicketCount() }}</div>
```

```typescript
protected urgentTicketCount = computed(() => 
  this.tickets().filter(t => t.status === 'open' && t.priority === 'high').length
);
```

## Services

### Service Structure
```typescript
@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root',
})
export class TicketService {
  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);
  private readonly apiUrl = '/api/v1/tickets';

  getTickets(projectId: string, filters?: TicketFilters): Observable<Ticket[]> {
    const params = this.buildParams(filters);
    return this.http.get<ApiResponse<Ticket[]>>(
      `/api/v1/projects/${projectId}/tickets`, 
      { params }
    ).pipe(map(res => res.data));
  }

  createTicket(projectId: string, dto: CreateTicketDto): Observable<Ticket> {
    return this.http.post<ApiResponse<Ticket>>(
      `/api/v1/projects/${projectId}/tickets`,
      dto
    ).pipe(map(res => res.data));
  }

  private buildParams(filters?: TicketFilters): HttpParams {
    let params = new HttpParams();
    if (filters?.status) {
      params = params.set('status', filters.status);
    }
    return params;
  }
}
```

### Service Best Practices
- Use `providedIn: 'root'` for singleton services
- Use `inject()` for dependencies
- Return Observables, let components subscribe
- Don't subscribe in services unless managing long-lived state

## State Management

### Use Signals for Component State
```typescript
export class TicketListComponent {
  protected tickets = signal<Ticket[]>([]);
  protected loading = signal(false);
  protected error = signal<string | null>(null);
  
  protected readonly hasTickets = computed(() => this.tickets().length > 0);
}
```

### Use Services with Signals for Shared State
```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class AuthStateService {
  private readonly _user = signal<User | null>(null);
  
  // Expose as readonly
  readonly user = this._user.asReadonly();
  readonly isAuthenticated = computed(() => this._user() !== null);
  readonly userDisplayName = computed(() => this._user()?.displayName ?? 'Guest');

  setUser(user: User | null): void {
    this._user.set(user);
  }

  clearUser(): void {
    this._user.set(null);
  }
}
```

## HTTP & Interceptors

### Functional Interceptors (Angular 17+)
```typescript
export const authInterceptor: HttpInterceptorFn = (req, next) => {
  const authState = inject(AuthStateService);
  const token = authState.token();
  
  if (token) {
    req = req.clone({
      setHeaders: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
    });
  }
  
  return next(req);
};

export const errorInterceptor: HttpInterceptorFn = (req, next) => {
  const router = inject(Router);
  const authState = inject(AuthStateService);
  
  return next(req).pipe(
    catchError((error: HttpErrorResponse) => {
      if (error.status === 401) {
        authState.clearUser();
        router.navigate(['/login']);
      }
      return throwError(() => error);
    }),
  );
};
```

## Forms

### Reactive Forms
```typescript
export class TicketFormComponent {
  private readonly fb = inject(FormBuilder);

  protected form = this.fb.nonNullable.group({
    title: ['', [Validators.required, Validators.maxLength(255)]],
    description: [''],
    priority: ['medium' as TicketPriority, Validators.required],
    assigneeId: [null as string | null],
  });

  protected onSubmit(): void {
    if (this.form.invalid) {
      this.form.markAllAsTouched();
      return;
    }
    
    const value = this.form.getRawValue();
    this.ticketService.createTicket(value).subscribe({
      next: () => this.router.navigate(['/tickets']),
      error: (err) => this.handleError(err),
    });
  }
}
```

## Routing

### Lazy Loading with Route Files
```typescript
// app.routes.ts
export const routes: Routes = [
  { path: '', redirectTo: 'projects', pathMatch: 'full' },
  {
    path: 'auth',
    loadChildren: () => import('./auth/auth.routes').then(m => m.AUTH_ROUTES),
  },
  {
    path: 'projects',
    loadChildren: () => import('./projects/projects.routes').then(m => m.PROJECT_ROUTES),
    canActivate: [authGuard],
  },
  {
    path: 'tickets',
    loadChildren: () => import('./tickets/tickets.routes').then(m => m.TICKET_ROUTES),
    canActivate: [authGuard],
  },
];
```

## Testing

### Component Tests with Angular Testing Library
```typescript
describe('TicketListComponent', () => {
  it('should display tickets', async () => {
    const mockTickets = [createMockTicket({ title: 'Test ticket' })];
    
    await render(TicketListComponent, {
      inputs: { projectId: 'proj-1' },
      providers: [
        { provide: TicketService, useValue: { getTickets: () => of(mockTickets) } },
      ],
    });

    expect(screen.getByText('Test ticket')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('should call saveTicket when save button clicked', async () => {
    const saveSpy = jest.fn().mockReturnValue(of({}));
    
    await render(TicketFormComponent, {
      providers: [
        { provide: TicketService, useValue: { createTicket: saveSpy } },
      ],
    });

    await userEvent.type(screen.getByLabelText('Title'), 'New ticket');
    await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /save/i }));

    expect(saveSpy).toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});
```

## Don'ts

- **Don't use `any`** — define proper types
- **Don't put complex logic in templates** — use computed signals
- **Don't use `ngClass`/`ngStyle`** — use `class`/`style` bindings
- **Don't organize folders by type** — organize by feature
- **Don't name handlers after events** — name them after actions (`saveTicket`, not `handleClick`)
- **Don't put long logic in lifecycle hooks** — extract to well-named methods
- **Don't mutate input values** — emit changes via outputs
- **Don't forget lifecycle interfaces** — `implements OnInit, OnDestroy`
- **Don't use constructor injection** — prefer `inject()` function
- **Don't expose template-only members as public** — use `protected`
